From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: full fences as a locked xchg on the stack, not MFENCE

Both translators lowered every full DMB/DSB and the store-load fence after STLR to MFENCE. MFENCE is dispatch-serializing on AMD Zen:
14.5 ns per fence on a Ryzen 5 5600 against 1.8 ns for `mov tmp, (%rsp); xchg tmp, (%rsp)` (a microbenchmark, 2026-11-19). PGR's
render thread was CPU-bound in menus (94% running, UnityMain waiting on it 86%), and half of its samples sat on 3-byte pairs in two
heavy regions of libunity.so built from DMB/LDAR/LDAXR/STLXR loops (Unity's lock-free queues). The xchg is a locked RMW of this
thread's own stack slot that writes back the value it read: it orders earlier stores before later loads like MFENCE for ordinary
memory and leaves EFLAGS alone (lock or/add would clobber the flags the heavy register allocator may keep live). Lite: EmitFullFence
(lite_translator_integer_ctrl.inc), used by DataMemoryBarrier and STLR; heavy: HeavyOptimizerFrontend::EmitFullFence, same uses.
Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.cc b/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.cc
index 350c585..7d69eaa 100644
--- a/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.cc
+++ b/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.cc
@@ -1846,7 +1846,7 @@ void HeavyOptimizerFrontend::LoadStoreExclusive(const Decoder::LoadStoreExclusiv
         return;
       }
       StoreUntagged(lss, base, 0, data);
-      GenRaw<x86_64::Mfence>();
+      EmitFullFence();  // apklayer patch (0075)
       return;
     }
 
@@ -2613,8 +2613,15 @@ void HeavyOptimizerFrontend::ClearExclusive() {
 }
 
 void HeavyOptimizerFrontend::DataMemoryBarrier() {
-  // Full DMB/DSB -> MFENCE: recover the StoreLoad ordering x86 TSO omits.
-  GenRaw<x86_64::Mfence>();
+  // Full DMB/DSB: recover the StoreLoad ordering x86 TSO omits.
+  EmitFullFence();  // apklayer patch (0075)
+}
+
+// apklayer patch (0075): as lite's EmitFullFence: `mov tmp, (%rsp); xchg tmp, (%rsp)` instead of MFENCE (dispatch-serializing on AMD
+// Zen, 8x the cost); a locked RMW that writes back the value it read, no EFLAGS.
+void HeavyOptimizerFrontend::EmitFullFence() {
+  Register tmp = std::get<0>(Gen<x86_64::MovqRegOp>({.base = x86_64::kMachineRegRSP}));
+  GenRaw<x86_64::XchgqRegOp>(tmp, {.base = x86_64::kMachineRegRSP});
 }
 
 void HeavyOptimizerFrontend::RecordBail(BailReason reason) {
diff --git a/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.h b/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.h
index 66bbcf2..3979d5e 100644
--- a/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.h
+++ b/cpu_emulation/heavy_optimizer/arm64/frontend.h
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ class HeavyOptimizerFrontend {
   // DMB/DSB full barrier: lowers to MFENCE (x86 TSO lacks StoreLoad ordering).
   // The store-only/load-only barrier variants are NOPed in the decoder.
   void DataMemoryBarrier();
+  void EmitFullFence();  // apklayer patch (0075)
 
   //
   // Immediate-form data processing.
diff --git a/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_int_carry_excl.inc b/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_int_carry_excl.inc
index d8c667a..d5ada30 100644
--- a/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_int_carry_excl.inc
+++ b/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_int_carry_excl.inc
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@
         if (!success()) return;
         if (args.rt >= 31) as_.Xorl(data, data);
         StoreUntagged(lss, base, 0, data);
-        as_.Mfence();
+        EmitFullFence();  // apklayer patch (0075)
         break;
       }
 
diff --git a/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_integer_ctrl.inc b/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_integer_ctrl.inc
index 064f862..22292b5 100644
--- a/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_integer_ctrl.inc
+++ b/cpu_emulation/lite_translator/arm64_to_x86_64/lite_translator_integer_ctrl.inc
@@ -1307,7 +1307,18 @@
   // DMB/DSB full barrier: x86 TSO lacks StoreLoad ordering, so a full guest
   // barrier must lower to MFENCE (the store-only/load-only variants are NOPed
   // upstream in the decoder).
-  void DataMemoryBarrier() { as_.Mfence(); }
+  void DataMemoryBarrier() { EmitFullFence(); }
+
+  // apklayer patch (0075): the full fence as `mov tmp, (%rsp); xchg tmp, (%rsp)`: a locked RMW of this thread's own stack slot that
+  // writes back what it read, orders earlier stores before later loads like MFENCE for ordinary memory, and leaves EFLAGS alone.
+  // MFENCE is dispatch-serializing on AMD Zen: 14.5 ns against 1.8 ns on a Ryzen 5 5600, and the hottest code of PGR's render thread
+  // (Unity's lock-free queues: DMB and STLR in a loop).
+  void EmitFullFence() {
+    Register tmp = AllocTempReg();
+    if (!success()) return;
+    as_.Movq(tmp, {.base = Assembler::rsp});
+    as_.Xchgq(tmp, {.base = Assembler::rsp});
+  }
 
   // IC IVAU, Xt — invalidate the translation cache for self-modified code. The
   // address is only known at run time, so end the region here and let the
